# Recipe: keep the bundled omi-audio, transcribe with another LOCAL engine.
# Audio never leaves your network. See README.md for what this changes and why.
#
# Apply: copy the uncommented lines into omi-host/.env, then
#   cd omi-host && docker compose up -d
#
# Any server that answers OpenAI's POST /v1/audio/transcriptions works:
# speaches (formerly faster-whisper-server), LocalAI, a whisper box on another PC.
# omi-audio keeps doing VAD, diarization, speaker embeddings and TTS; it hands
# the engine one finished utterance at a time.

OMI_ASR_ENGINE=openai

# Base URL up to and including /v1, as seen from INSIDE the omi-audio container:
# a LAN IP, or a container name if the engine runs on the same Docker network.
# "localhost" here means the omi-audio container itself, not this machine.
OMI_ASR_URL=http://192.168.20.10:8001/v1

# Model id exactly as the engine names it (GET <OMI_ASR_URL>/models lists them).
# speaches downloads nothing on its own; fetch the model once first:
#   curl -X POST http://192.168.20.10:8001/v1/models/Systran/faster-whisper-large-v3
OMI_ASR_MODEL=Systran/faster-whisper-large-v3

# Only if the engine was started with an API key (speaches: API_KEY=...).
# OMI_ASR_API_KEY=

# "en" by default. "auto" lets the engine detect the language per utterance.
# OMI_ASR_LANGUAGE=en

# Running speaches on this same host? omi-local already owns port 8000, so
# publish it elsewhere (CPU image shown; speaches also ships CUDA images):
#   docker run -d --name speaches --restart unless-stopped -p 8001:8000 \
#     ghcr.io/speaches-ai/speaches:latest-cpu

# Spoken replies can come from the same engine instead of Piper, if it serves
# POST /v1/audio/speech. Model and voice as that engine names them.
# OMI_TTS_ENGINE=openai
# OMI_TTS_URL=http://192.168.20.10:8001/v1
# OMI_TTS_MODEL=
# OMI_TTS_VOICE=

# No AMD gfx906 card on this host? Diarization runs fine on the CPU; also add
# no-gpu.override.yml so the container doesn't ask for /dev/kfd and /dev/dri.
# OMI_DIA_DEVICE=cpu
